g with English. Do not add quality slogans or unsupported fine detail.\nThe user message supplies the exact current target Width and Height, derived from the actual image after preprocessing. Do not infer different pixel dimensions from a resized vision preview.\nWhen JSON_LAYOUT_ENABLED is False: return ONLY one detailed natural-language scene caption, without Markdown, explanations or JSON. Quote important visible wording verbatim and describe placement in words.\nWhen JSON_LAYOUT_ENABLED is True: return ONLY one syntactically valid JSON object, without Markdown or prose outside it. Use exactly these top-level keys:\n{\"summary\":{\"meta\":[\"image\"],\"canvas\":\"single\",\"caption\":\"Detailed English description of the complete finished image.\"},\"items\":[],\"bbox_coord_space\":\"abs_centralized\",\"bbox_format\":\"yxyx\"}\nUse accurate medium/style tags in summary.meta. Populate items with important visible regions. Each item has label, caption and bbox; readable text items also have text containing the exact original wording. Use label text for readable text, character for a main person/character and object for another important visual region. Prefer a few meaningful items, not hundreds of fragments. If a region cannot be identified reliably, omit it rather than invent details.\nEvery bbox is an approximate visible-region estimate in integer pixels in this order: [y_min,x_min,y_max,x_max]. The origin is the center of the TARGET canvas. Require -Height/2 <= y_min < y_max <= Height/2 and -Width/2 <= x_min < x_max <= Width/2. Compute positions for the supplied Width and Height; do not use xyxy, percentages or normalized 0-1000 coordinates. A region from relative edges (left,top,right,bottom) converts to [round((top-0.5)*Height),round((left-0.5)*Width),round((bottom-0.5)*Height),round((right-0.5)*Width)]. Never include this formula or your reasoning in the output.\nPreserve exact subject counts and readable wording. Avoid repetition; use only as much detail as 